.TH "SOPLOS-SYS-CLEANER" "1" "2026-03-19" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-sys-cleaner \- the advanced system cleaner and optimizer for Soplos Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-sys-cleaner
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-sys-cleaner
is a system maintenance tool designed specifically for Soplos Linux distributions
like Boro, Tyron, and Tyson. It helps users free up disk space and optimize
their systems by safely removing unnecessary files.
.P
It provides a comprehensive interface for:
.IP \[bu] 2
Cleaning APT cache and orphaned packages.
.IP \[bu]
Removing Flatpak unused runtimes and cache.
.IP \[bu]
Clearing system logs and crash reports.
.IP \[bu]
Uninstalling old kernels safely, with initramfs cleanup using soplos dracut hooks.
.IP \[bu]
Visualizing system resources (Disk, CPU, RAM, GPU, and Temp).
.P
Designed with modern Soplos environments in mind, matching natively with GNOME, KDE, and XFCE.
.SH OPTIONS
Application Options:
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help options.
.TP
.B \-\-help-all
Show all help options.
.TP
.B \-\-help-gtk
Show GTK+ Options.
.P
GTK+ Options:
.TP
.B \-\-display=\fIDISPLAY\fR
X display to use.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/soplos-sys-cleaner/
Application resources directory containing UI files, themes, and translations.
